# 1. Professional Practice and Ethics (NCE content outline, 12%): 24 items
CAT = "nceEthics"; SEG = "ETH"
Q = [
("Under the ACA Code of Ethics (2014), how long must a counselor wait before a romantic relationship with a former client?",
 "Five years", ["Two years", "One year", "Seven years"],
 "Standard A.5.c bars sexual or romantic relationships with former clients for five years after the last professional contact, and even then the counselor must show the relationship is not exploitative."),
("A client who cannot afford fees offers to repair the counselor's fence in exchange for sessions. Under the ACA Code, bartering is acceptable only if:",
 "The client asks and it is not exploitative", ["The counselor alone sets the item's value", "It covers no more than half the fee", "The client's family approves of it"],
 "Standard A.10.e allows bartering when the relationship is not exploitative or harmful, the client requests it, and it is an accepted practice in the community. The arrangement is put in a written contract."),
("When deciding whether to accept a gift from a client, which factor does the ACA Code ask the counselor to weigh?",
 "The client's motive for giving", ["The counselor's financial need", "The agency's yearly gift budget", "The gift's later resale value"],
 "Standard A.10.f asks counselors to consider the therapeutic relationship, the monetary value of the gift, the client's motivation for giving and the counselor's motivation for accepting or declining."),
("A counselor believes a diagnosis would harm a client and the client does not need one for services. Under the ACA Code, the counselor may:",
 "Refrain from making a diagnosis", ["Assign the mildest code", "Ask the client to pick one", "Diagnose without telling the client"],
 "Standard E.5.d allows counselors to refrain from making or reporting a diagnosis if they believe it would cause harm to the client or others. They still keep honest records."),
("A counselor licensed in one state starts video sessions with a client who has moved to another state. What must the counselor check first?",
 "The laws of both states", ["Only her own state's law", "Only the client's insurer", "Only the video platform's rules"],
 "Standard H.1.b says counselors providing distance counseling must follow the laws and regulations of both the counselor's practice location and the client's place of residence."),
("Under the ACA Code, how should a counselor handle social media?",
 "Separate professional and personal pages", ["Accept friend requests from clients", "Post client successes with their names", "Use a single page for every contact"],
 "Standard H.6.a asks counselors who keep a professional online presence to separate it from their personal web pages and profiles, which limits dual relationships online."),
("During the first group session, what should the counselor tell members about confidentiality?",
 "The leader cannot guarantee it", ["It is fully protected by state law", "It binds only the group leader", "It ends on the last group day"],
 "Standard B.4.a asks group leaders to explain the importance and limits of confidentiality for the group. The leader is bound by it, but other members are not bound the same way, so the leader cannot promise that everyone will keep it."),
("A client has met every counseling goal and is no longer benefiting from sessions. The ACA Code says the counselor should:",
 "End services with pre-termination counseling", ["Continue weekly sessions with no end date", "Stop sessions without discussion", "Lower the fee to keep the client"],
 "Standard A.11.c directs counselors to end a relationship when the client no longer needs or benefits from it, offering pre-termination counseling and referrals as needed."),
("A counselor is leaving her agency next month. What protects her clients from abandonment?",
 "Planning transfers and continued care", ["Ending all cases on her last day", "Letting clients find new providers", "Moving all her clients to her new practice"],
 "Standard A.12 bars abandoning or neglecting clients, and A.11.d asks that transfers keep open communication with clients and the new practitioners. A leaving counselor plans transfers and makes sure care continues."),
("Which situation describes counselor impairment that calls for stepping back from practice?",
 "Grief that clouds her judgment", ["A disagreement with a colleague", "A full schedule of weekly clients", "Starting a new specialty training"],
 "Standard C.2.g asks counselors to watch for signs of impairment from their own physical, mental or emotional problems and refrain from offering services when impaired, seeking help as needed."),
("A school counselor's 14-year-old client discloses vague worries. The parents ask for details of the sessions. The counselor should FIRST:",
 "Balance privacy with parents' rights", ["Refuse to speak with the parents", "Give the parents full session notes", "End counseling with the student"],
 "Standard B.5.b recognizes that parents have legal rights over minors while the counselor protects the minor's confidential information. Counselors work to build collaborative relationships with parents, guided by state law."),
("A counselor wants to see a client's records from a previous therapist. What is required first?",
 "The client's written consent", ["A request from the insurer", "A phone call to the therapist", "A note from the counselor's supervisor"],
 "Records are released to third parties only with the client's written authorization, except where law requires disclosure (standard B.6.g)."),
("A counselor wants to take on a client from a population she has never served. What does competence require?",
 "Training and supervision first", ["A larger caseload of such clients", "A sliding fee scale for that group", "A statement on her own website"],
 "Standard C.2.b lets counselors practice in new specialty areas only after appropriate education, training and supervised experience, while protecting clients from harm."),
("A client who uses a wheelchair cannot reach the counselor's second-floor office. What should the counselor do?",
 "Arrange an accessible location", ["Refer the client to another state", "Offer only email sessions", "Charge for the extra effort"],
 "Counselors provide reasonable accommodations for clients with disabilities, consistent with the Americans with Disabilities Act, such as an accessible ground-floor room."),
("A counselor plans a study comparing two groups of clients. Before collecting data she must get approval from:",
 "An institutional review board", ["The clients' health insurers", "The state counseling licensing board", "A national professional association"],
 "An institutional review board reviews research with human participants to protect their rights and welfare before data are collected."),
("A researcher concludes a treatment works when in truth it has no effect. This is a:",
 "Type I error", ["Type II error", "Sampling error", "Measurement error"],
 "A Type I error rejects a null hypothesis that is actually true, a false positive. Its probability is set by alpha. A Type II error misses a real effect."),
("Which statistic is best for comparing the mean scores of three different treatment groups?",
 "Analysis of variance", ["Independent samples t-test", "Chi-square test of independence", "Pearson correlation coefficient"],
 "ANOVA compares the means of three or more groups at once. A t-test compares two means, and chi-square compares frequencies of categories."),
("Clients are sorted only by whether they attended group or not and whether they relapsed or not. Which test fits these data?",
 "Chi-square test", ["Paired t-test", "Analysis of variance", "Multiple regression"],
 "Chi-square tests whether two categorical variables are related, using counts in each cell. The t-test and ANOVA need a continuous outcome."),
("A correlation of r = -0.82 between hours of sleep and anxiety scores shows a:",
 "Strong negative relationship", ["Weak negative relationship", "Strong positive relationship", "Proof that sleep cuts anxiety"],
 "The sign gives direction and the size gives strength, so -0.82 is strong and inverse: more sleep goes with lower anxiety. Correlation alone does not prove cause."),
("In a positively skewed distribution of client income, which measure of central tendency is highest?",
 "The mean", ["The median", "The mode", "The range"],
 "A few very high values pull the mean toward the tail, so in a positive skew the mean is above the median, which is above the mode."),
("Clients in a study improve partly because a new clinic opened nearby during the study. This threat to internal validity is:",
 "History", ["Maturation", "Regression", "Attrition"],
 "History is an outside event during the study that could explain the change. Maturation is change from natural growth or aging within the participants."),
("A counselor needs to document a session for the record. Which part of a SOAP note holds the counselor's clinical impressions?",
 "Assessment", ["Subjective", "Objective", "Plan section"],
 "In SOAP notes, Subjective is what the client reports, Objective is what the counselor observes, Assessment is the counselor's clinical impression and Plan is the next steps."),
("A counselor is unsure how to handle a client's new disclosure of a complex legal issue. The ethical step is to:",
 "Consult a colleague or supervisor", ["Decide alone and move on quickly", "Ask the client for some legal advice", "Post the case in an online forum"],
 "When facing an unclear ethical or clinical problem, counselors consult colleagues or supervisors while protecting client identity, and document the consultation."),
("Which part of an informed consent discussion is required at the start of counseling?",
 "Fees and billing arrangements", ["The counselor's home address", "The counselor's personal history", "The other clients' diagnoses"],
 "Standard A.2.b lists items clients must be told, including the purposes, risks, benefits and limits of counseling, the counselor's credentials, fees and billing, and the limits of confidentiality."),
]
